Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@gmail.com> writes:

> At the moment I'm planning on attempting to ascend a weaponless, vegan 
> monk. After reading http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/monk_faq.html, it 
> seems that weaponless monks don't do that much in damage.
> 
> Right now the only plans I have are to outfit a monk with gauntlets of 
> power, a highly enchanted ring of increase damage and kicking boots. 
> Unfortunately kicking boots make speed a problem. I'm not inclined to rely 
> upon potions of speed. Are the bonuses provided by kicking boots worthy 
> enough to forego speed boots?
> 
> Any suggestions?

Get a dragon scale mail.  Yes, it makes you 'clumsy', but a 
grand master in martial arts performs quite well even as 
'clumsy', and the armor will reduce the damage taken significantly.  
I don't think the extra kick of the kicking boots will compensate 
for the loss of speed, so I'd prefer the speed boots.  Remember 
that extra speed also means more possibilities for life-saving 
actions (think Demogorgon).  For the big ones, I suggest to have 
some potions of paralysis ready (wield them while wearing a ring 
of free action), as well as some wands of death; it is painful to 
have Rodney double-troubled while going weaponless in my experience.  

IIRC, you can also eat rings of increase damage if they're of an 
edible sort in your game and get extra damage, but this usually 
requires quite a polypile festival and hence a lot of patience.  

